  "task": {
    "objective": "Supply each polity's opposite-bank outpost twice before any outpost defense reaches zero; manage couriers, fuel, relay information and timed passage agreements.",
    "natural_termination": "Failure when any defense is zero after pressure. Otherwise success when every outpost has at least two deliveries. If these coincide, defense loss prevents success; both are natural completion, with natural causes taking priority over H.",
    "interaction": "One polity's offer changes another's legal council choices; acceptance creates temporary pass access and access to the grantor's powered beacon information. Supply investments compete with delivering and defending each polity's outpost.",
    "observation_access": "Partially observable. Every role sees Manhattan radius two around its courier and radius three around its own powered relays or relays owned by a polity currently granting it passage. Other roles' couriers, cargo and home stocks are masked outside revealed cells; owned home and owned beacon telemetry remain known. Public outposts/defenses, pass locations/owners, pending offers, accepted agreement timers and specified public events are broadcast. The world map declares map_visible and never public=true. Hidden map/objects are -1 in the flat observation with explicit visibility bits. Role renderers bind the same masks; hidden blocked-move events and unrevealed refuel events are not public event channels."
